course: dictionary
lesson: 3738
title: Flora and the plants of a place
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Flora is a noun. Its main meaning is all the plants that grow in one place or at one time. You can often work it out from the words around it. Look for «flora and fauna», which means the plants and animals of a place. Fauna means animals, so flora must mean plants.
explain: «The class recorded the local flora on their nature walk.» Read the clues: a nature walk is outside, and local means nearby. So the class wrote down the plants that grow near them. Swap in your meaning: «the class wrote down the plants that grow near them» still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Look at capital letters too. «Flora was also the Roman goddess of flowers.» Flora with a capital F is a name, not a plant. A story about a girl called Flora is a clue that the word is a name. Always check whether the word is a name before you guess its meaning.
fact: Flora means all the plants that grow in a particular place or at a particular time.
fact: «Flora and fauna» means the plants and animals of a place, such as the flora and fauna of Australia.
fact: The word flora comes from Latin «flos», which means flower.
fact: Flora with a capital F can be a girl's name. Flora was also the Roman goddess of flowers.
fact: «Gut flora» means the tiny living things, especially bacteria, that live inside a part of the body.
exercise: «The class recorded the local flora on their nature walk.» What does flora mean here? | Stones and soil under our feet | The weather on that day | *The plants that grow in that place | The animals that live in the pond
exercise: Mia reads «the flora and fauna of the island». Fauna means animals. What does flora mean? | Clouds | Stones | Rivers | *Plants
exercise: In a story, «Flora walked into the room and sat down.» What is Flora here? | A plant | A kind of rock | A goddess of animals | *A girl's name
test: «Gut flora» means tiny living things inside a part of the body. What kind of living things are they, especially? | Flowers | Huge animals | *Tiny living things, especially bacteria | Rocks
test: Where does the word flora come from? | A word for stone | A word for tree | *Latin «flos», meaning flower | A word for water
exam: Ben says flora and fauna both mean animals. Is he right? | No: both mean rocks | Yes, both mean animals | Flora means animals and fauna means plants | *No: flora means plants and fauna means animals
